Z||000003||Carrolles||07-03-2001||01:52 PM||||Have you tried squirting some WD-40 into the lock?<P>The little spring is what closes the small cover to keep weather out of the lock.  If the little cover is **** -eyed in there the spring could have come loose.  If so just reach in and grab the spring with a needle nose pliers and yank it out.<P>The passenger side lock on my 85GT did this.  The key would not go into the lock.  The cover and spring were floating around inside the lock.  I pulled them out and it works fine now.  However I now have to keep it hosed down with WD-40 to keep the weather out.||||reg||1
